WEBVTT

00:00:37.370 --> 00:00:38.894
Sick Bay to the Captain.

00:00:38.938 --> 00:00:40.496
This is the Doctor speaking.

00:00:40.540 --> 00:00:42.098
You've brought us out of stasis.

00:00:42.142 --> 00:00:43.336
I assume you have news.

00:00:43.376 --> 00:00:45.241
Yes.

00:00:45.278 --> 00:00:47.007
Our sensors show
your vital signs are normal.

00:00:47.047 --> 00:00:48.173
How are you feeling?

00:00:48.214 --> 00:00:50.682
We're fine.
How long were we in stasis?

00:00:50.717 --> 00:00:52.685
A total of 17 days.

00:00:52.719 --> 00:00:54.152
That long?

00:00:54.187 --> 00:00:57.020
I wanted to exhaust every
possibility of finding a cure.

00:00:57.090 --> 00:00:58.216
And?

00:00:58.258 --> 00:01:02.092
I regret to inform you
that I have been unsuccessful.

00:01:02.128 --> 00:01:05.689
I have not been able to develop
a counteragent for the virus,

00:01:05.732 --> 00:01:08.530
and I have no other options
to explore.

00:01:08.568 --> 00:01:11.833
What about keeping us
in stasis aboard Voyager?

00:01:11.871 --> 00:01:13.600
Something
in the planet's environment

00:01:13.640 --> 00:01:15.904
is shielding you
from the effects of the virus.

00:01:15.942 --> 00:01:18.968
If you leave, you risk
a recurrence of the disease,

00:01:19.012 --> 00:01:20.570
which would undoubtedly
prove fatal.

00:01:20.613 --> 00:01:22.808
The only option I can think of
at the moment

00:01:22.849 --> 00:01:24.976
is contacting the Vidiians.

00:01:25.051 --> 00:01:26.882
They have sophisticated
medical technology.

00:01:26.920 --> 00:01:29.388
It's possible
they might be able to help.

00:01:29.422 --> 00:01:31.856
We'll take it under advisement,
Doctor.

00:01:31.891 --> 00:01:33.825
Thank you for your efforts.
Janeway out.

00:01:33.860 --> 00:01:34.952
What do you think?

00:01:34.994 --> 00:01:36.291
It's risky.

00:01:36.329 --> 00:01:38.763
The Vidiians have never shown
any willingness to help us.

00:01:38.798 --> 00:01:40.663
It's more likely
they'd attack Voyager

00:01:40.700 --> 00:01:42.895
and try to harvest body parts
from the crew.

00:01:42.936 --> 00:01:43.903
Agreed.

00:01:43.937 --> 00:01:44.995
I just want to make sure

00:01:45.105 --> 00:01:47.266
we're not overlooking
a possible alternative.

00:01:47.307 --> 00:01:48.968
Could we live with ourselves,

00:01:49.008 --> 00:01:51.772
knowing we'd sent Voyager
into that kind of danger?

00:01:55.381 --> 00:01:57.008
Janeway to Tuvok.

00:01:57.117 --> 00:01:58.516
I'm here, Captain.

00:01:58.551 --> 00:02:01.850
You must be aware
of the Doctor's report.

00:02:01.888 --> 00:02:02.946
Yes.

00:02:02.989 --> 00:02:07.050
I'm turning over command
of the ship to you

00:02:07.093 --> 00:02:08.219
on a permanent basis.

00:02:08.261 --> 00:02:11.230
Your orders are to resume
a course for the Alpha Quadrant.

00:02:11.264 --> 00:02:13.755
And regardless
of the Doctor's suggestion,

00:02:13.800 --> 00:02:16.894
you are not to make contact
with the Vidiians.

00:02:16.936 --> 00:02:19.097
I understand.

00:02:19.139 --> 00:02:21.471
I'll prepare a message
for the crew.

00:04:12.251 --> 00:04:15.743
So we're just going
to abandon them on this planet?

00:04:15.788 --> 00:04:18.222
Those were Captain Janeway's
express orders.

00:04:18.257 --> 00:04:19.588
But you're Captain now.

00:04:19.625 --> 00:04:20.853
You can rescind them.

00:04:20.893 --> 00:04:22.383
To what end?

00:04:22.428 --> 00:04:24.396
I can't believe
we haven't been able

00:04:24.430 --> 00:04:26.330
to find a cure
for an insect bite.

00:04:26.365 --> 00:04:29.061
The Doctor hasn't deactivated
himself for a month.

00:04:29.101 --> 00:04:30.728
He's tried everything.

00:04:30.770 --> 00:04:31.964
He's searched every database,

00:04:32.037 --> 00:04:34.130
attempted
the most drastic research.

00:04:34.173 --> 00:04:35.538
You can't fault him.

00:04:35.574 --> 00:04:38.975
I can tell you the morale
of the crew is going to suffer

00:04:39.078 --> 00:04:40.841
if we leave them behind.

00:04:40.880 --> 00:04:42.711
Not if, Mr. Neelix.

00:04:42.748 --> 00:04:44.272
When we leave them behind.

00:04:44.316 --> 00:04:45.783
The decision has been made.

00:04:45.818 --> 00:04:46.785
We will, of course,

00:04:46.819 --> 00:04:48.980
provide them
with everything they'll need

00:04:49.054 --> 00:04:50.988
for their survival and comfort.

00:04:51.023 --> 00:04:52.684
I am arranging
for a modular shelter

00:04:52.725 --> 00:04:54.590
to be transported
to the surface.

00:04:54.627 --> 00:04:56.754
They'll have all the technology
they need...

00:04:56.796 --> 00:04:59.993
weapons, tricorders,
a replicator.

00:05:00.065 --> 00:05:02.556
You talk as though
it were a camping trip.

00:05:02.601 --> 00:05:05.263
They have to spend the rest
of their lives down there.

00:05:05.304 --> 00:05:06.931
That is not a certainty.

00:05:06.972 --> 00:05:10.135
Captain Janeway intends to
continue researching the virus.

00:05:10.176 --> 00:05:12.144
She is an able scientist,

00:05:12.178 --> 00:05:14.646
and may eventually be able
to effect a cure.

00:05:14.680 --> 00:05:17.376
They have a type-9 shuttlecraft
at their disposal,

00:05:17.416 --> 00:05:19.475
if it becomes possible
for them to leave the planet.

00:05:19.518 --> 00:05:23.716
A type-9 shuttlecraft has
a top speed of warp 4.

00:05:23.756 --> 00:05:27.886
It won't take them more than...
oh, about 700 years to get home.

00:05:27.927 --> 00:05:31.488
I am not certain what it is
you expect me to do, Lieutenant.

00:05:31.530 --> 00:05:35.591
I guess, clearly,
something you can't do,

00:05:35.634 --> 00:05:38.865
which is to feel as rotten
about this as we do.

00:05:38.904 --> 00:05:43.170
You are correct that I am unable
to experience that emotion.

00:05:43.209 --> 00:05:46.110
And frankly, I fail to see
what the benefit would be.

00:05:47.413 --> 00:05:50.143
If there is nothing more,
you are all dismissed.

00:06:06.232 --> 00:06:07.893
Janeway to Tuvok.

00:06:07.933 --> 00:06:08.922
Yes, Captain?

00:06:09.001 --> 00:06:10.434
We've received the transport.

00:06:10.469 --> 00:06:12.767
We'll check it over and let you
know if we're missing anything.

00:06:13.772 --> 00:06:16.138
I will remain in orbit
until I hear from you.

00:06:16.175 --> 00:06:18.939
And, after that, we can still
remain in communication

00:06:18.978 --> 00:06:20.411
for approximately 36 hours.

00:06:20.446 --> 00:06:22.471
I'll contact you
before the day is over.

00:06:22.515 --> 00:06:23.777
Janeway out.

00:06:23.816 --> 00:06:26.410
It looks like they transported
the contents of the whole ship.

00:06:26.452 --> 00:06:28.181
We may have to be here
for a while.

00:06:28.220 --> 00:06:31.553
Petri dishes, protein analyzer,
DNA sequencers.

00:06:31.590 --> 00:06:33.490
Everything I need
for my research is here.

00:06:33.526 --> 00:06:35.426
Do you really think
you can find a cure?

00:06:35.461 --> 00:06:37.622
It may take a while,
but, yes, I do.

00:06:37.663 --> 00:06:40.427
If I can find a specimen
of the insect that infected us,

00:06:40.466 --> 00:06:42.764
I can begin analyzing
protein cofactors.

00:06:42.801 --> 00:06:44.564
That might give us
the information we need

00:06:44.603 --> 00:06:46.298
to find out what it is
in this environment

00:06:46.338 --> 00:06:48.306
that's keeping us
from being sick

00:06:48.340 --> 00:06:49.500
and how to replicate it.

00:06:52.912 --> 00:06:54.971
Does it matter
which way these things go?

00:06:55.014 --> 00:06:56.208
I guess it depends
whether you're

00:06:56.248 --> 00:06:57.840
in a beige mood or a gray mood.

00:06:57.883 --> 00:06:59.282
That's not much of a choice.

00:06:59.318 --> 00:07:00.876
Couldn't Starfleet have come up

00:07:00.920 --> 00:07:02.182
with something
a little more cheerful?

00:07:02.221 --> 00:07:04.086
Like polka dots?

00:07:04.123 --> 00:07:05.886
I was thinking more
of a tasteful pinstripe,

00:07:05.925 --> 00:07:07.654
something in blues and greens.

00:07:09.361 --> 00:07:10.385
Well, I suggest we put

00:07:10.429 --> 00:07:12.590
the gray on the outside
and the beige inside.

00:07:12.631 --> 00:07:13.598
I like that.

00:07:13.632 --> 00:07:15.532
I've always looked better
in beige.

00:07:15.568 --> 00:07:17.229
Actually, it might
be kind of interesting,

00:07:17.269 --> 00:07:18.293
roughing it for a while.

00:07:18.337 --> 00:07:19.463
"Roughing it"?

00:07:19.505 --> 00:07:20.665
Let's see.

00:07:20.706 --> 00:07:23.766
We have shelter, furniture,
research equipment,

00:07:23.809 --> 00:07:26.209
tricorders, a replicator.

00:07:26.245 --> 00:07:27.371
It's too rough for me.

00:07:27.413 --> 00:07:28.505
We don't have a bathtub.

00:07:28.547 --> 00:07:29.514
A bathtub?

00:07:29.548 --> 00:07:30.515
I love a bath.

00:07:30.549 --> 00:07:31.948
It's my favorite way
of relaxing.

00:07:32.051 --> 00:07:34.611
Captain, I'm sure you can learn
to love the sonic shower.

00:07:34.653 --> 00:07:36.848
You know, Chakotay,
it occurs to me,

00:07:36.889 --> 00:07:39.585
we aren't exactly
in a command structure anymore.

00:07:39.625 --> 00:07:41.456
Maybe you should call me
Kathryn.

00:07:45.297 --> 00:07:47.424
Give me a few days on that one,
okay?

00:07:49.735 --> 00:07:51.726
This diagnostic report
looks like it was written

00:07:51.770 --> 00:07:53.931
by a first-year Academy cadet.

00:07:55.040 --> 00:07:56.598
There are mistakes.

00:07:58.410 --> 00:08:00.173
It's incomplete.

00:08:00.212 --> 00:08:01.907
I'm sorry, Lieutenant.

00:08:01.947 --> 00:08:03.539
I guess I've been distracted.

00:08:03.582 --> 00:08:05.174
We've all been distracted,
Ensign.

00:08:05.217 --> 00:08:06.411
That's no excuse.

00:08:06.452 --> 00:08:08.249
Yes, ma'am.

00:08:11.590 --> 00:08:13.114
I can't get anything done here.

00:08:13.158 --> 00:08:14.648
Nobody can concentrate.

00:08:14.693 --> 00:08:16.593
I know how they feel.

00:08:16.629 --> 00:08:19.120
I'm not feeling
so terrific myself,

00:08:19.164 --> 00:08:21.223
but I don't let that
get in the way of my work.

00:08:23.769 --> 00:08:25.396
B'Elanna...

00:08:30.743 --> 00:08:33.940
I've been talking with some
of the Starfleet crew.

00:08:34.013 --> 00:08:37.346
They're not happy
about what happened.

00:08:37.383 --> 00:08:39.374
I was wondering...

00:08:39.418 --> 00:08:40.817
how are the Maquis taking it?

00:08:40.853 --> 00:08:43.083
How do you think
they're taking it?

00:08:43.122 --> 00:08:46.819
This isn't a Starfleet issue,
Harry.

00:08:46.859 --> 00:08:48.053
It's affecting everyone.

00:08:48.093 --> 00:08:50.391
Then why don't we
do something about it?

00:08:50.429 --> 00:08:52.226
Do what?

00:08:52.264 --> 00:08:53.959
I don't know.

00:08:56.068 --> 00:08:59.162
It seems like we shouldn't
just accept this.

00:08:59.204 --> 00:09:00.432
Well, that's all well and good,

00:09:00.472 --> 00:09:03.032
but, frankly, I can't think
of anything else we can do.

00:09:03.075 --> 00:09:05.908
If you have any ideas,
I'll listen.

00:09:05.978 --> 00:09:09.175
Otherwise, I think we should
take a deep breath and move on.

00:09:23.462 --> 00:09:24.429
Catch anything?

00:09:24.463 --> 00:09:26.158
Just the same ones as yesterday,

00:09:26.198 --> 00:09:29.258
and they don't seem to carry
the pathogen that's infected us.

00:09:29.301 --> 00:09:30.461
Where have you been?

00:09:30.502 --> 00:09:31.469
Oh, in the woods.

00:09:31.503 --> 00:09:32.527
For the past two days,

00:09:32.571 --> 00:09:34.368
you've been spending
a lot of time in the woods.

00:09:34.406 --> 00:09:35.930
Is something going on
I should know about?

00:09:36.008 --> 00:09:36.940
Uh, not yet.

00:09:37.009 --> 00:09:37.941
Not yet?

00:09:38.010 --> 00:09:39.272
What's that supposed to mean?

00:09:39.311 --> 00:09:41.302
It means, when it's time
for you to know, I'll tell you.

00:09:41.346 --> 00:09:42.677
Don't I even get hints?

00:09:42.715 --> 00:09:44.842
I'm building something.

00:09:44.883 --> 00:09:47.044
Building?

00:09:47.086 --> 00:09:48.519
What could you be building?

00:09:48.554 --> 00:09:50.818
And why can't you tell me?

00:09:50.856 --> 00:09:52.517
You can't stand it, can you?

00:09:52.558 --> 00:09:54.219
You're like a little kid,
wheedling.

00:09:54.259 --> 00:09:55.817
Tuvok to Janeway.

00:09:55.861 --> 00:09:57.590
Janeway here.

00:09:57.629 --> 00:10:00.393
We're about to move
out of communications range.

00:10:00.432 --> 00:10:02.627
How are you faring?

00:10:04.503 --> 00:10:06.095
We're doing quite well.

00:10:06.138 --> 00:10:09.266
I'd like to speak
to the crew now.

00:10:09.308 --> 00:10:13.108
Your com link has been
put through to the entire ship.

00:10:21.186 --> 00:10:23.677
This is Kathryn Janeway.

00:10:23.722 --> 00:10:25.417
I've never liked
saying good-bye,

00:10:25.457 --> 00:10:26.788
so I'll make this brief.

00:10:28.026 --> 00:10:30.494
But I want you all to know
that serving as your Captain

00:10:30.529 --> 00:10:34.158
has been the most extraordinary
experience of my life.

00:10:34.199 --> 00:10:37.657
No Captain could ask more
than what this crew has given...

00:10:37.703 --> 00:10:41.366
bravery, compassion
and strength of character.

00:10:41.406 --> 00:10:44.239
But I think what I'll miss most
is the fun.

00:10:44.276 --> 00:10:47.734
The times we joked together,
the games on the holodeck.

00:10:47.780 --> 00:10:50.442
I'll remember the laughter
more than anything.

00:10:50.482 --> 00:10:52.245
Although Commander Chakotay
and I won't be with you

00:10:52.284 --> 00:10:54.275
for the rest of your journey,

00:10:54.319 --> 00:10:57.720
we know that you'll be the same
steadfast crew for Mr. Tuvok

00:10:57.756 --> 00:10:59.587
as you have been for us.

00:10:59.625 --> 00:11:02.958
We wish you a safe
and a speedy journey home.

00:11:02.995 --> 00:11:04.963
Our thoughts will be with you.

00:11:05.063 --> 00:11:07.054
Janeway out.

00:11:07.099 --> 00:11:09.966
Thank you, Captain, Commander.

00:11:10.068 --> 00:11:12.969
I am sure I speak
for the entire crew when I say

00:11:13.071 --> 00:11:16.700
we will always remember
your grace and courage.

00:11:16.742 --> 00:11:18.505
And I would like to add,

00:11:18.544 --> 00:11:20.944
it has been an honor
serving with you.

00:11:20.979 --> 00:11:23.743
Live long and prosper.

00:11:29.721 --> 00:11:34.749
Kathryn Janeway's Personal Log,
Stardate 49690.1.

00:11:34.792 --> 00:11:38.819
Day 24 of our stay on the planet
we've named New Earth.

00:11:38.863 --> 00:11:40.694
As yet, I've been unable
to make any progress

00:11:40.732 --> 00:11:42.996
in finding a cure
for our illness,

00:11:43.101 --> 00:11:45.001
but a soak
in the tub Chakotay built

00:11:45.069 --> 00:11:48.095
always helps me focus
on possible solutions.

00:11:48.139 --> 00:11:49.902
Chakotay, are you there?

00:11:49.941 --> 00:11:51.932
No, I left an hour ago.

00:11:51.976 --> 00:11:54.171
I was thinking.

00:11:54.212 --> 00:11:56.407
Maybe looking
for protein cofactors

00:11:56.447 --> 00:11:58.005
is the wrong approach.

00:11:58.116 --> 00:11:59.208
Even if I can't find

00:11:59.250 --> 00:12:01.684
a specimen of the insect
that infected us...

00:12:01.719 --> 00:12:03.482
I could try to learn something

00:12:03.521 --> 00:12:07.048
about the biomolecular evolution
of this planet's ecosystem.

00:12:07.091 --> 00:12:08.922
Can't hurt to give it a try.

00:12:13.031 --> 00:12:13.963
Chakotay!

00:12:14.032 --> 00:12:14.964
What?

00:12:15.033 --> 00:12:16.057
Someone's in the woods.

00:12:23.041 --> 00:12:24.235
Over there.

00:12:28.513 --> 00:12:31.539
It looks like
some kind of primate.

00:12:31.582 --> 00:12:33.812
I've detected primate
life-signs here,

00:12:33.851 --> 00:12:35.318
but I've never seen one.

00:12:35.353 --> 00:12:37.583
Hello.

00:12:41.325 --> 00:12:43.225
Are you hungry?

00:12:43.261 --> 00:12:45.889
Is that why you came here?

00:12:49.000 --> 00:12:50.433
I'm Kathryn.

00:12:50.468 --> 00:12:51.992
He's Chakotay.

00:12:52.103 --> 00:12:54.333
We've had to move
into your neighborhood,

00:12:54.372 --> 00:12:56.465
but I hope we can be friends.

00:13:00.545 --> 00:13:03.275
Oh. Maybe he'll come back.

00:13:03.314 --> 00:13:05.407
Looking for a pet?

00:13:05.450 --> 00:13:06.815
No. Looking for a clue

00:13:06.851 --> 00:13:09.319
about primate physiology
on this planet.

00:13:09.353 --> 00:13:12.049
They must have to contend
with insect bites, too.

00:13:16.994 --> 00:13:19.588
Well... excuse me.

00:13:35.413 --> 00:13:37.973
Maybe we should be out
looking for other primates.

00:13:38.049 --> 00:13:40.381
I might be missing
something important.

00:13:45.056 --> 00:13:46.387
Kathryn...

00:13:47.825 --> 00:13:49.087
the Doctor worked for weeks

00:13:49.127 --> 00:13:51.288
trying to find a treatment
for this disease.

00:13:51.329 --> 00:13:52.353
Yes.

00:13:52.396 --> 00:13:53.886
You've been at it
12 hours a day,

00:13:53.931 --> 00:13:55.558
seven days a week
since we got here,

00:13:55.600 --> 00:13:57.591
and we're still
no closer to a cure

00:13:57.635 --> 00:13:59.865
than we were the day
we were infected.

00:13:59.904 --> 00:14:02.930
I'm not sure
what you're getting at.

00:14:04.675 --> 00:14:06.939
My people have a saying.

00:14:07.044 --> 00:14:10.605
"Even the eagle
must know when to sleep."

00:14:10.648 --> 00:14:13.549
Maybe it's time
we both considered that.

00:14:13.584 --> 00:14:14.573
You mean quit.

00:14:14.619 --> 00:14:15.608
Give up.

00:14:15.653 --> 00:14:18.679
Why do you have
to see it as defeat?

00:14:18.723 --> 00:14:20.520
Maybe it's simply...

00:14:20.558 --> 00:14:23.721
accepting what life
has dealt us,

00:14:23.761 --> 00:14:25.626
finding the good in it.

00:14:30.468 --> 00:14:34.461
There may be a day when I'll
come to that, Chakotay, but...

00:14:34.505 --> 00:14:37.303
I'm a long way
from it right now.

00:14:37.341 --> 00:14:39.332
I need to keep looking.

00:14:54.792 --> 00:14:56.987
Acting Captain's Log,
supplemental.

00:14:57.094 --> 00:14:58.584
After six weeks, the decision

00:14:58.629 --> 00:15:01.393
to leave Captain Janeway
and the First Officer behind

00:15:01.432 --> 00:15:03.627
still seems to weigh heavily
on the crew.

00:15:05.536 --> 00:15:07.094
Captain Tuvok?

00:15:07.138 --> 00:15:08.332
Yes, Ensign?

00:15:08.372 --> 00:15:12.604
I'm picking up a convoy
on long-range sensors.

00:15:12.643 --> 00:15:14.508
It's Vidiian, sir.

00:15:14.545 --> 00:15:16.410
Distance?

00:15:16.447 --> 00:15:19.143
Approximately 1.5 light-years.

00:15:19.183 --> 00:15:22.482
Lieutenant, alter course
to a different heading.

00:15:22.520 --> 00:15:24.715
I don't want to risk
their detecting us.

00:15:26.157 --> 00:15:28.318
Sir, the Vidiians...

00:15:28.359 --> 00:15:29.417
Yes?

00:15:29.460 --> 00:15:31.121
They're within hailing range.

00:15:31.162 --> 00:15:32.720
We could ask them
if they know anything

00:15:32.763 --> 00:15:34.253
about the Captain's illness.

00:15:34.298 --> 00:15:35.697
You're aware
that Captain Janeway

00:15:35.733 --> 00:15:38.964
specifically told us not
to risk contacting the Vidiians?

00:15:39.036 --> 00:15:43.166
Yes, but it's not like we went
out of our way to find them.

00:15:43.207 --> 00:15:45.801
We would just be
taking advantage

00:15:45.843 --> 00:15:48.368
of an opportunity
that's presented itself.

00:15:48.412 --> 00:15:51.973
That bit of sophistry is not
terribly persuasive, Ensign.

00:15:52.049 --> 00:15:57.988
Sir, how can we turn our backs
on this chance to do something?

00:15:58.022 --> 00:15:59.785
Don't we have to try?

00:15:59.824 --> 00:16:02.918
Don't we owe that to the Captain
and the Commander?

00:16:02.960 --> 00:16:04.655
The matter is closed, Ensign.

00:16:04.695 --> 00:16:06.094
Return to your station.

00:16:10.668 --> 00:16:12.101
What's wrong
with the rest of you?

00:16:12.136 --> 00:16:14.229
You know I'm right.

00:16:14.272 --> 00:16:15.466
Ensign Kim.

00:16:15.506 --> 00:16:17.201
We have a chance to help them.

00:16:17.241 --> 00:16:18.765
How can we ignore that?

00:16:18.809 --> 00:16:21.607
Ensign, you are
relieved of duty.

00:16:21.646 --> 00:16:22.635
Leave the Bridge at once,

00:16:22.680 --> 00:16:24.147
or I will have you
put in the brig.

00:16:28.185 --> 00:16:29.174
Harry...

00:16:41.532 --> 00:16:43.466
Proceed on the altered course,
Lieutenant.

00:16:54.578 --> 00:16:57.479
Excuse me, Ensign Kim.

00:16:57.515 --> 00:16:58.982
Could we?

00:16:59.016 --> 00:17:00.745
Sure. Have a seat.

00:17:04.055 --> 00:17:05.215
We just wanted you to know,

00:17:05.256 --> 00:17:07.417
we heard what happened
on the Bridge.

00:17:07.458 --> 00:17:08.720
And we think
you're absolutely right.

00:17:08.759 --> 00:17:10.420
We've got to contact
the Vidiians.

00:17:10.461 --> 00:17:12.429
It's a risk, but it's worth it.

00:17:12.463 --> 00:17:14.431
That's what I think,

00:17:14.465 --> 00:17:16.797
but Captain Tuvok's
made his decision.

00:17:16.834 --> 00:17:19.530
Two Ensigns and a crewman
won't change his mind.

00:17:19.570 --> 00:17:21.367
There are a lot more
who agree with us.

00:17:21.405 --> 00:17:22.633
A lot.

00:17:22.673 --> 00:17:24.231
Really?

00:17:24.275 --> 00:17:25.799
Everyone we talk to
can't believe

00:17:25.843 --> 00:17:27.435
that Tuvok won't
give this a try.

00:17:29.080 --> 00:17:30.138
Come on.

00:17:34.785 --> 00:17:36.685
Did you hear what happened
this morning?

00:17:36.721 --> 00:17:37.710
Sure did.

00:17:37.755 --> 00:17:40.451
Three weeks ago,
you said if I had an idea

00:17:40.491 --> 00:17:42.391
about what to do, you'd listen.

00:17:42.426 --> 00:17:44.724
I'm listening.

00:17:44.762 --> 00:17:48.493
Is there something going on
that I should know about?

00:17:48.532 --> 00:17:50.523
Have a seat, Neelix.

00:17:50.568 --> 00:17:52.866
We might have come up
with the biggest morale booster

00:17:52.903 --> 00:17:54.097
you could possibly imagine.

00:18:04.815 --> 00:18:05.839
Come in.

00:18:10.621 --> 00:18:11.986
Could I have a moment, sir?

00:18:15.593 --> 00:18:18.061
It's 0100 hours, Ensign.

00:18:18.095 --> 00:18:20.120
Don't you have
the early shift this morning?

00:18:20.164 --> 00:18:22.394
Yes, sir, but this is important.

00:18:22.433 --> 00:18:24.367
Very well.

00:18:28.572 --> 00:18:31.769
First of all,
I want to apologize

00:18:31.809 --> 00:18:33.674
for my behavior yesterday.

00:18:33.711 --> 00:18:35.372
Apology accepted.

00:18:35.413 --> 00:18:38.582
I understand that this is
a difficult situation for you.

00:18:38.715 --> 00:18:41.650
I'd like to suggest a plan.

00:18:41.685 --> 00:18:43.915
It's something a lot of people
have helped to develop.

00:18:47.023 --> 00:18:48.684
We have
two big bargaining points

00:18:48.725 --> 00:18:50.955
when it comes to dealing
with the Vidiians.

00:18:51.027 --> 00:18:54.690
First, there's the woman
Doc treated... Danara Pel.

00:18:54.731 --> 00:18:55.823
They were very close,

00:18:55.865 --> 00:18:57.958
so I'm sure she'd help us
if she could;

00:18:58.001 --> 00:19:00.435
and then there's B'Elanna.

00:19:00.470 --> 00:19:03.496
Her DNA might lead to a cure
for the phage.

00:19:03.540 --> 00:19:07.533
We could offer them some...
in exchange for their help

00:19:07.577 --> 00:19:10.102
with a cure
for the Captain and Chakotay.

00:19:10.146 --> 00:19:14.742
Those are, as you say,
points in our favor,

00:19:14.784 --> 00:19:16.877
but there is also the fact
that we

00:19:16.920 --> 00:19:18.785
were recently responsible
for the destruction

00:19:18.822 --> 00:19:22.724
of a Vidiian ship,
an act which killed over 300

00:19:22.759 --> 00:19:24.021
of their people.

00:19:24.060 --> 00:19:27.257
That alone makes it unwise
for us to contact them.

00:19:30.133 --> 00:19:31.794
Sir...

00:19:31.835 --> 00:19:33.097
I think you should know

00:19:33.136 --> 00:19:35.730
how many people on this ship
disagree with you.

00:19:35.772 --> 00:19:39.606
Everyone I talked to thinks
we should give this a try.

00:19:39.643 --> 00:19:41.076
The people you talked to

00:19:41.111 --> 00:19:43.944
do not have the responsibility
of commanding this vessel.

00:19:44.047 --> 00:19:45.947
I do.

00:19:46.049 --> 00:19:48.449
The safety of this crew
is paramount,

00:19:48.485 --> 00:19:51.386
and I must do whatever I can
to ensure that safety.

00:19:51.421 --> 00:19:54.288
But if we're willing
to take that risk in order

00:19:54.324 --> 00:19:55.416
to help the Captain...

00:19:55.458 --> 00:19:59.952
Ensign, I'm going to say this
once and once only.

00:19:59.996 --> 00:20:02.487
If you ever question
my orders again,

00:20:02.532 --> 00:20:04.898
you will be relieved
of duty permanently.

00:20:04.934 --> 00:20:06.629
The next words

00:20:06.670 --> 00:20:10.470
I expect to hear from you
are, "yes, sir."

00:20:15.445 --> 00:20:16.412
Yes...

00:20:16.446 --> 00:20:18.107
sir.

00:20:33.296 --> 00:20:36.390
I'm going to check the
insect traps in beta-4.

00:20:36.433 --> 00:20:39.095
Oh, what are you up to now?

00:20:40.704 --> 00:20:41.898
Making headboards.

00:20:41.938 --> 00:20:43.337
Headboards?

00:20:43.373 --> 00:20:46.365
I've noticed you sometimes
sit up in your bed to read.

00:20:46.409 --> 00:20:49.810
Figured you might as well
have a comfortable backrest.

00:20:49.846 --> 00:20:51.905
That's very thoughtful
of you, Chakotay.

00:20:51.948 --> 00:20:53.347
You've done so many things

00:20:53.383 --> 00:20:55.010
to make our lives
easier here.

00:20:55.051 --> 00:20:56.848
The cooking, for example.

00:20:56.886 --> 00:20:58.353
I hate to cook.

00:21:01.257 --> 00:21:05.125
But what I do makes you
uncomfortable, doesn't it?

00:21:06.496 --> 00:21:07.656
Every time I do something

00:21:07.697 --> 00:21:11.292
that adds a personal touch
to the shelter, you resist it.

00:21:12.469 --> 00:21:15.199
Sometimes it feels...

00:21:15.238 --> 00:21:17.297
as though you've given up.

00:21:17.340 --> 00:21:19.240
That you're focused
on making a home here

00:21:19.275 --> 00:21:21.800
instead of finding a cure
that will let us leave.

00:21:21.845 --> 00:21:23.938
I can't sacrifice the present

00:21:23.980 --> 00:21:26.346
waiting for a future
that may never happen.

00:21:26.382 --> 00:21:30.250
The reality of this situation
is that we may never leave here.

00:21:30.286 --> 00:21:33.687
So, yes, I'm trying
to make a home...

00:21:33.723 --> 00:21:38.023
something that's more
than a plain gray box.

00:21:40.330 --> 00:21:42.696
Someday I may have to let go.

00:21:42.732 --> 00:21:46.463
But not today, okay?

00:21:46.503 --> 00:21:49.301
I tried a new glucose
bait in the traps.

00:21:49.339 --> 00:21:51.239
I have a feeling

00:21:51.274 --> 00:21:53.071
this might be the day
I make a breakthrough.

00:22:11.628 --> 00:22:13.528
Hello?

00:22:13.563 --> 00:22:14.996
Chakotay?

00:22:48.464 --> 00:22:49.863
Hello again.

00:22:53.203 --> 00:22:56.434
Well, you certainly
cover a lot of territory.

00:22:57.507 --> 00:22:59.270
Or are you following me?

00:23:02.846 --> 00:23:04.336
Do you understand me?

00:23:07.550 --> 00:23:09.347
There.

00:23:09.385 --> 00:23:11.285
Know what that is?

00:23:11.321 --> 00:23:13.414
That little insect just might be

00:23:13.456 --> 00:23:15.720
what gets me
out of your backyard.

00:23:15.758 --> 00:23:17.658
What do you think of that, huh?

00:23:25.301 --> 00:23:26.529
What is it?

00:23:31.474 --> 00:23:33.533
What's happened to the sky?

00:23:35.578 --> 00:23:39.275
If you're suggesting I should
get out of here, I agree.

00:23:56.399 --> 00:23:57.593
Oh!

00:24:03.539 --> 00:24:04.767
Oh!

00:24:11.180 --> 00:24:12.545
Kathryn!

00:24:14.050 --> 00:24:15.711
Kathryn.

00:24:15.752 --> 00:24:17.310
Are you hurt?

00:24:17.353 --> 00:24:20.220
No. I couldn't keep my balance
and carry the case.

00:24:20.256 --> 00:24:21.314
Give it to me.

00:24:21.357 --> 00:24:23.188
What's happening?

00:24:23.226 --> 00:24:25.786
It seems to be some
kind of plasma storm.

00:24:25.828 --> 00:24:27.853
Our tricorders
don't recognize it,

00:24:27.897 --> 00:24:29.865
but it sure packs a wallop.

00:24:48.418 --> 00:24:50.113
Come in.

00:24:51.220 --> 00:24:52.517
Do you have a moment?

00:24:52.555 --> 00:24:54.420
Of course.

00:24:54.457 --> 00:24:55.856
Please sit down.

00:24:55.892 --> 00:24:59.760
I'd like to talk to you...
about my father.

00:24:59.796 --> 00:25:00.990
Your father?

00:25:01.097 --> 00:25:03.224
He was a very wise man.

00:25:03.266 --> 00:25:07.032
More than anyone,
he shaped the person I am.

00:25:07.070 --> 00:25:08.332
If it hadn't been for him,

00:25:08.371 --> 00:25:10.862
I would have never questioned
my people's beliefs.

00:25:10.907 --> 00:25:12.772
I would have never
left our city.

00:25:12.809 --> 00:25:14.538
I would never have met
all of you.

00:25:14.577 --> 00:25:16.636
Then we owe him a debt.

00:25:16.679 --> 00:25:19.739
It is difficult to imagine
this journey without you.

00:25:19.782 --> 00:25:22.751
When he died,
I had just turned one year old.

00:25:22.785 --> 00:25:24.946
I didn't know
how I'd get through

00:25:24.988 --> 00:25:27.115
the rest of my life without him,

00:25:27.156 --> 00:25:28.885
but then I started
working with you

00:25:28.925 --> 00:25:30.859
and I didn't miss him
so much anymore.

00:25:32.095 --> 00:25:34.563
I am honored by the comparison.

00:25:34.597 --> 00:25:35.859
As Captain,

00:25:35.898 --> 00:25:38.128
the well-being of your crew
is important to you.

00:25:38.167 --> 00:25:39.930
Of course.

00:25:41.938 --> 00:25:43.405
Their emotional well-being

00:25:43.439 --> 00:25:45.304
as well as
their physical safety?

00:25:46.676 --> 00:25:50.510
I cannot allow myself to become
hostage to their feelings.

00:25:50.546 --> 00:25:53.915
Tuvok, they are suffering
because of this.

00:25:54.048 --> 00:25:55.743
Maybe you don't know
what it's like.

00:25:55.783 --> 00:25:57.842
If you are suggesting

00:25:57.885 --> 00:25:59.785
that I am not sensitive
to the situation,

00:25:59.820 --> 00:26:02.254
nothing could be further
from the truth.

00:26:03.624 --> 00:26:06.787
I have lost a valued friend.

00:26:06.827 --> 00:26:10.285
I am not immune to the effects
of that loss.

00:26:10.331 --> 00:26:12.561
Then try to imagine
what it's like

00:26:12.600 --> 00:26:15.228
for those of us
who feel things deeply.

00:26:15.269 --> 00:26:17.499
A lot of the crew
are on the Bridge,

00:26:17.538 --> 00:26:19.130
hoping you'll talk to them.

00:26:36.057 --> 00:26:37.422
None of you can appreciate

00:26:37.458 --> 00:26:39.688
what it means to be
in command of a ship

00:26:39.727 --> 00:26:42.696
until that responsibility
rests squarely on your shoulders

00:26:42.730 --> 00:26:44.925
as it does on mine.

00:26:44.966 --> 00:26:47.560
It has been suggested
that I take an action,

00:26:47.601 --> 00:26:49.967
which would require me
to disobey an order,

00:26:50.037 --> 00:26:53.700
and knowingly put this crew into
a life-threatening situation.

00:26:53.741 --> 00:26:56.972
In general, I believe it
demonstrates faulty leadership

00:26:57.044 --> 00:27:00.480
to be guided by the emotions
of a distraught crew.

00:27:00.514 --> 00:27:04.917
However, as Captain,
I must not ignore

00:27:05.019 --> 00:27:08.182
the sensibilities
of those I command.

00:27:08.222 --> 00:27:11.123
We will contact the Vidiians.

00:27:11.158 --> 00:27:14.184
This is my decision
and mine alone.

00:27:14.228 --> 00:27:18.187
You are all absolved
of responsibility in the matter.

00:27:18.232 --> 00:27:21.395
I will accept any consequences
which may ensue.

00:27:21.435 --> 00:27:24.734
Lieutenant, set a course
for the Vidiian convoy.

00:27:26.974 --> 00:27:29.841
Mr. Kim, let me know
when we're within hailing range.

00:27:53.100 --> 00:27:55.330
Oh! Oh, no!

00:28:04.278 --> 00:28:05.802
Let's check outside.

00:28:05.846 --> 00:28:08.610
Maybe some of the insect traps
are still intact.

00:28:32.173 --> 00:28:34.767
None of this
is salvageable either.

00:28:40.481 --> 00:28:43.575
There's no way I can
continue to do my research.

00:28:45.653 --> 00:28:47.120
I'm sorry.

00:28:52.993 --> 00:28:55.427
Well, that's one way
of letting go.

00:29:01.001 --> 00:29:05.131
Captain's Log, Stardate 49694.2.

00:29:05.172 --> 00:29:07.003
We have contacted
the Vidiian convoy

00:29:07.041 --> 00:29:08.702
with encouraging results.

00:29:08.742 --> 00:29:11.267
They have promised to
communicate with Dr. Danara Pel

00:29:11.312 --> 00:29:13.872
and ask if she will help us.

00:29:13.914 --> 00:29:16.474
Sir, the Vidiians
are hailing us.

00:29:16.517 --> 00:29:17.779
On screen.

00:29:19.687 --> 00:29:21.518
Hello, Lieutenant.

00:29:21.555 --> 00:29:22.920
Doctor Pel,

00:29:22.990 --> 00:29:24.890
I didn't expect
to see you this quickly.

00:29:24.925 --> 00:29:27.587
When I heard what happened, I
boarded the first ship I could.

00:29:27.628 --> 00:29:29.391
Tell me about this illness.

00:29:29.430 --> 00:29:32.729
They were infected by a virus
after being bitten by insects

00:29:32.766 --> 00:29:35.394
on a planet approximately
70 light-years from here

00:29:35.436 --> 00:29:37.927
in a system
with a yellow dwarf star.

00:29:38.005 --> 00:29:40.098
The third planet
in a system of seven?

00:29:40.141 --> 00:29:41.073
Yes.

00:29:41.108 --> 00:29:42.075
I know it well.

00:29:42.109 --> 00:29:43.542
There's a particular kind

00:29:43.577 --> 00:29:45.943
of burrowing insect
that carries the disease.

00:29:45.980 --> 00:29:48.778
Years ago, we developed an
antiviral agent to combat it.

00:29:48.816 --> 00:29:50.681
Can we get some from you?

00:29:50.718 --> 00:29:53.778
Of course. Our Captain said
we could rendezvous with you.

00:29:53.821 --> 00:29:55.584
He's transmitted
the coordinates.

00:29:56.557 --> 00:29:57.455
I have them, sir.

00:29:57.491 --> 00:29:58.958
Thank you, Doctor.

00:29:59.026 --> 00:30:00.425
We appreciate your help.

00:30:00.461 --> 00:30:03.055
I'm glad I can be of assistance.

00:30:03.097 --> 00:30:05.224
Estimated time
to the coordinates?

00:30:05.266 --> 00:30:07.700
Approximately 20 hours.

00:30:07.735 --> 00:30:10.363
Until then, I want
a series of battle drills.

00:30:10.404 --> 00:30:12.895
We must be ready
for whatever comes.

00:30:14.942 --> 00:30:15.966
I've been thinking...

00:30:16.043 --> 00:30:18.341
there's plenty of wood
available here.

00:30:18.379 --> 00:30:20.677
I could probably add
rooms to the shelter.

00:30:20.714 --> 00:30:22.409
Give us a little more
living space.

00:30:22.449 --> 00:30:23.939
How would you mill it?

00:30:23.984 --> 00:30:25.975
I could do a certain
amount with a phaser,

00:30:26.020 --> 00:30:28.318
but I was actually
thinking of logs.

00:30:28.355 --> 00:30:30.448
As in log cabin?

00:30:30.491 --> 00:30:32.652
I built a few of them
when I was growing up.

00:30:32.693 --> 00:30:35.628
My father thought it was
important that I learn how.

00:30:35.663 --> 00:30:38.632
When I was young, my parents
took us on backpacking trips.

00:30:38.666 --> 00:30:39.690
They thought we should all

00:30:39.733 --> 00:30:41.325
keep a connection
to our pioneer roots.

00:30:41.368 --> 00:30:44.303
I hated it...
no bed, no replicator...

00:30:44.338 --> 00:30:46.704
- No bathtub.
- No bathtub.

00:30:46.740 --> 00:30:50.437
I guess I was always a child
of the 24th century.

00:30:50.477 --> 00:30:53.571
Well...
maybe those camping trips

00:30:53.614 --> 00:30:55.479
helped prepare you
for life here.

00:30:55.516 --> 00:30:57.006
Oh, no.

00:30:57.084 --> 00:30:58.984
Life here is much better
than that.

00:31:01.555 --> 00:31:02.886
I think that's the first time

00:31:02.923 --> 00:31:05.448
I've heard you say anything
positive about being here.

00:31:10.297 --> 00:31:12.322
Well, hello there.

00:31:12.366 --> 00:31:14.300
I haven't seen you in a while.

00:31:14.335 --> 00:31:15.529
Where have you been?

00:31:17.371 --> 00:31:18.565
Do you expect him to answer you?

00:31:18.606 --> 00:31:19.698
Not really.

00:31:19.740 --> 00:31:21.207
I just sense
intelligence in him,

00:31:21.242 --> 00:31:23.073
and I could swear
he came to warn me

00:31:23.110 --> 00:31:24.338
about the plasma storm.

00:31:24.378 --> 00:31:25.572
Come here, fella.

00:31:25.613 --> 00:31:27.103
Come on.

00:31:30.517 --> 00:31:32.451
I doubt that he
can be domesticated...

00:31:32.486 --> 00:31:33.885
at least not very easily.

00:31:36.223 --> 00:31:40.250
Well, we have plenty of time.

00:31:40.294 --> 00:31:43.092
The rest of our lives.

00:31:46.000 --> 00:31:47.490
That's a long time.

00:31:49.203 --> 00:31:51.034
At least I hope so.

00:31:52.273 --> 00:31:53.934
Well, I can't give you
orders anymore,

00:31:53.974 --> 00:31:56.204
but I suggest we get
back to work.

00:31:56.243 --> 00:31:57.335
Aye, aye, Captain.

00:32:08.489 --> 00:32:11.185
I guess I'm not used
to that kind of work.

00:32:13.494 --> 00:32:16.429
My knots are getting knots.

00:32:19.633 --> 00:32:20.895
Here, let me help.

00:32:36.884 --> 00:32:38.852
Oh, that feels good.

00:32:41.822 --> 00:32:43.915
I've had a lot
of practice at this.

00:32:43.957 --> 00:32:47.518
My mother used to get
sore necks all the time.

00:32:47.561 --> 00:32:50.621
I was the only one she'd trust
not to make it worse.

00:33:14.620 --> 00:33:15.746
That's much better.
Thank you.

00:33:18.157 --> 00:33:21.718
Well... I'm going
to go to bed now.

00:33:21.760 --> 00:33:22.954
I'll see you in the morning.

00:33:23.062 --> 00:33:25.496
Sleep well, Kathryn.

00:33:25.531 --> 00:33:27.829
Yes.

00:33:27.867 --> 00:33:29.425
You, too.

00:34:25.724 --> 00:34:26.691
Got something.

00:34:26.725 --> 00:34:30.320
Vidiian ship,
bearing 325 mark 5.

00:34:30.362 --> 00:34:31.727
Hail them.

00:34:33.065 --> 00:34:34.430
They aren't responding.

00:34:34.466 --> 00:34:36.263
Trying
on alternating frequencies.

00:34:36.302 --> 00:34:39.169
I'm reading a second ship,
177 mark 5.

00:34:39.204 --> 00:34:41.604
I've got it.
Now a third.

00:34:41.640 --> 00:34:42.971
They're surrounding us.

00:34:43.042 --> 00:34:45.306
None of them are answering hails

00:34:45.344 --> 00:34:46.936
and their weapons are powered.

00:34:46.979 --> 00:34:48.241
Red Alert.

00:35:04.663 --> 00:35:06.756
We have to talk about this.

00:35:08.934 --> 00:35:10.333
All right.

00:35:11.971 --> 00:35:15.168
I think we need to define
some parameters...

00:35:15.207 --> 00:35:17.402
about us.

00:35:17.443 --> 00:35:21.504
I'm not sure I can...
define parameters.

00:35:23.882 --> 00:35:26.077
But I can tell you a story...

00:35:26.118 --> 00:35:29.019
an ancient legend
among my people.

00:35:31.957 --> 00:35:34.482
It's about an angry warrior

00:35:34.526 --> 00:35:35.493
who lived his life

00:35:35.527 --> 00:35:37.290
in conflict
with the rest of his tribe...

00:35:37.329 --> 00:35:39.490
a man who couldn't find peace,

00:35:39.531 --> 00:35:41.658
even with the help
of his spirit guide.

00:35:44.370 --> 00:35:48.363
For years, he struggled
with his discontent.

00:35:48.407 --> 00:35:51.399
But the only satisfaction
he ever got

00:35:51.443 --> 00:35:54.139
came when he was in battle.

00:35:54.179 --> 00:35:56.739
This made him a hero
among his tribe,

00:35:56.782 --> 00:36:00.343
but the warrior still longed
for peace within himself.

00:36:00.386 --> 00:36:02.820
One day, he and his war party

00:36:02.855 --> 00:36:06.018
were captured
by a neighboring tribe

00:36:06.058 --> 00:36:08.288
led by a woman warrior.

00:36:08.327 --> 00:36:11.592
She called on him to join her

00:36:11.630 --> 00:36:14.622
because her tribe was too small
and weak to defend itself

00:36:14.667 --> 00:36:15.793
from all its enemies.

00:36:15.834 --> 00:36:18.928
The woman warrior
was brave and beautiful

00:36:18.971 --> 00:36:20.336
and very wise.

00:36:21.740 --> 00:36:24.265
The angry warrior
swore to himself...

00:36:25.978 --> 00:36:27.707
that he would stay by her side,

00:36:27.746 --> 00:36:31.341
doing whatever he could
to make her burden lighter.

00:36:31.383 --> 00:36:34.250
From that point on,
her needs would come first.

00:36:36.555 --> 00:36:38.250
And in that way...

00:36:40.592 --> 00:36:43.459
the warrior began to know...

00:36:43.495 --> 00:36:45.156
the true meaning of peace.

00:36:50.235 --> 00:36:52.430
Is that really...

00:36:52.471 --> 00:36:54.905
an ancient legend?

00:36:59.878 --> 00:37:01.573
No.

00:37:03.582 --> 00:37:06.107
But that made it easier to say.

00:37:36.882 --> 00:37:38.110
Shields down to 58 percent.

00:37:38.150 --> 00:37:41.244
Rearm the forward phaser
array and fire at will.

00:37:41.286 --> 00:37:42.412
Firing.

00:37:43.889 --> 00:37:46.483
Shields down to 47 percent.

00:37:46.525 --> 00:37:48.493
Sir, there are just
too many of them.

00:37:48.527 --> 00:37:49.824
Load aft torpedo bays.

00:37:51.230 --> 00:37:52.629
Torpedoes armed.

00:37:52.664 --> 00:37:53.722
Fire number one.

00:37:59.404 --> 00:38:00.336
Report.

00:38:00.372 --> 00:38:01.839
They're still coming.

00:38:03.075 --> 00:38:04.667
Fire number two.

00:38:05.778 --> 00:38:07.211
Tuvok to Engineering.

00:38:07.246 --> 00:38:08.304
Torres here, sir.

00:38:08.347 --> 00:38:10.372
Listen carefully.

00:38:15.487 --> 00:38:17.114
She has a broken arm.

00:38:17.156 --> 00:38:18.783
Set it
with the osteogenic stimulator.

00:38:18.824 --> 00:38:20.519
I think there's someone
on the monitor.

00:38:20.559 --> 00:38:21.548
This way.

00:38:21.593 --> 00:38:24.687
Odd. Why wouldn't they
just use the com line?

00:38:26.331 --> 00:38:27.798
I don't think this is coming
from our ship.

00:38:27.833 --> 00:38:28.891
Shmullus...

00:38:28.934 --> 00:38:30.902
Shmullus, can you hear me?

00:38:32.237 --> 00:38:33.204
Danara.

00:38:33.238 --> 00:38:35.536
Shmullus,
I have to do this quickly.

00:38:35.574 --> 00:38:37.371
I'm on one of the Vidiian ships.

00:38:38.877 --> 00:38:40.469
Do they know
you're contacting me?

00:38:40.512 --> 00:38:41.604
Are you in any danger?

00:38:41.647 --> 00:38:44.616
No. Everyone's too focused
on the battle.

00:38:46.118 --> 00:38:50.646
Oh, Shmullus, I swear I didn't
know they planned to attack.

00:38:50.689 --> 00:38:53.658
I thought we were on
an errand of mercy.

00:38:53.692 --> 00:38:54.659
I believe you.

00:38:54.693 --> 00:38:56.524
I have the antiviral serum here.

00:38:56.562 --> 00:38:58.325
If you could use your
transporter to get it to your...

00:38:58.363 --> 00:38:59.330
Our shields are up.

00:38:59.364 --> 00:39:00.831
We can't transport anything
through them.

00:39:01.900 --> 00:39:03.891
I don't know what else
to suggest.

00:39:03.936 --> 00:39:06.598
All right.
I'll see what I can do.

00:39:06.638 --> 00:39:08.538
Maybe we can lower the shields

00:39:08.574 --> 00:39:10.166
long enough
to transport the serum.

00:39:10.209 --> 00:39:12.074
Sick Bay to Bridge.

00:39:14.079 --> 00:39:15.546
This is Tuvok.

00:39:15.581 --> 00:39:16.843
We're rather busy here, Doctor.

00:39:16.882 --> 00:39:18.873
Doctor Pel is on
one of the Vidiian ships.

00:39:18.917 --> 00:39:20.441
If we can drop
our shields briefly,

00:39:20.485 --> 00:39:21.884
we can beam aboard the serum.

00:39:21.920 --> 00:39:24.286
Keep this com line open, Doctor.

00:39:24.323 --> 00:39:26.188
When you hear me
order the shields down,

00:39:26.225 --> 00:39:28.693
you must complete a site-to-site
transport yourself.

00:39:28.727 --> 00:39:30.592
We will be busy
with the Vidiians.

00:39:30.629 --> 00:39:31.926
Understood.

00:39:31.997 --> 00:39:33.191
Bridge to Engineering.

00:39:33.232 --> 00:39:34.256
Report.

00:39:34.299 --> 00:39:35.926
We're ready to eject
the antimatter container.

00:39:36.001 --> 00:39:37.696
Stand by for my command.

00:39:37.736 --> 00:39:39.761
Here is the sequence of events.

00:39:39.805 --> 00:39:42.672
We will drop shields
to transport the medicine.

00:39:42.708 --> 00:39:43.936
At the same moment,

00:39:43.976 --> 00:39:45.944
the antimatter container
will be ejected.

00:39:46.011 --> 00:39:47.171
As soon as it's clear,

00:39:47.212 --> 00:39:49.703
Mr. Kim will detonate it
with a photon torpedo.

00:39:49.748 --> 00:39:53.184
Simultaneously, Mr. Paris
will jump to full impulse,

00:39:53.218 --> 00:39:55.311
so that we will not take
the brunt of the explosion.

00:39:55.354 --> 00:39:57.447
Is everyone clear on this?

00:39:57.489 --> 00:39:59.684
Timing is
of the utmost importance.

00:39:59.725 --> 00:40:01.893
We won't get a second chance.

00:40:02.026 --> 00:40:03.050
Understood.

00:40:03.094 --> 00:40:04.220
Aye, sir.

00:40:04.262 --> 00:40:05.320
We're ready down here.

00:40:05.363 --> 00:40:06.853
Doctor?

00:40:06.898 --> 00:40:08.092
I've set up
to make the transport.

00:40:08.132 --> 00:40:09.224
Stand ready, then.

00:40:12.503 --> 00:40:15.267
Lower shields.

00:40:15.306 --> 00:40:17.297
Initiating transport.

00:40:17.341 --> 00:40:19.707
Ejecting
the antimatter container...

00:40:19.744 --> 00:40:21.143
now.

00:40:23.881 --> 00:40:25.143
We've got it.

00:40:25.182 --> 00:40:26.979
Raise shields.

00:40:27.084 --> 00:40:29.075
Mr. Kim, Mr. Paris?

00:40:29.120 --> 00:40:30.587
Go.

00:40:30.621 --> 00:40:32.088
Firing torpedo.

00:40:39.363 --> 00:40:40.694
Report.

00:40:40.731 --> 00:40:42.164
The Vidiian ships
are all disabled, sir.

00:40:42.199 --> 00:40:43.461
They're not pursuing.

00:40:43.501 --> 00:40:45.526
Ready to go to warp, sir.

00:40:46.537 --> 00:40:47.799
Set a course for the planet

00:40:47.838 --> 00:40:50.136
where we left the Captain
and Commander Chakotay.

00:40:50.174 --> 00:40:51.368
Warp 6.

00:40:51.409 --> 00:40:53.104
Aye, aye, sir.

00:41:17.668 --> 00:41:18.828
How are they coming?

00:41:21.238 --> 00:41:22.705
Very nicely.

00:41:22.740 --> 00:41:25.300
We should have vine-ripened
Talaxian tomatoes

00:41:25.343 --> 00:41:26.970
in a couple of months...

00:41:27.011 --> 00:41:29.809
unless this planet has
the equivalent of tomato bugs.

00:41:29.847 --> 00:41:31.678
Oh, they're awful.

00:41:31.716 --> 00:41:34.981
I would never have thought
of you as a gardener.

00:41:35.052 --> 00:41:38.249
Hmm. I grew up around farmers.

00:41:38.289 --> 00:41:41.588
My parents insisted we learn
some basic gardening skills.

00:41:41.625 --> 00:41:42.922
Did you hate that
as much as camping?

00:41:42.960 --> 00:41:44.154
Of course.

00:41:44.195 --> 00:41:46.220
Who wanted to muck around
in the dirt

00:41:46.263 --> 00:41:48.663
when you could be studying
quantum mechanics?

00:41:49.734 --> 00:41:54.171
But... I find it
very satisfying now,

00:41:54.205 --> 00:41:57.038
watching the seeds sprout
and grow.

00:41:59.410 --> 00:42:01.002
If your tomatoes
could spare you for a minute,

00:42:01.045 --> 00:42:03.605
I'd like your opinion
on something in the house.

00:42:03.647 --> 00:42:05.114
You've come
to the right person.

00:42:05.149 --> 00:42:06.480
I always have an opinion.

00:42:06.517 --> 00:42:07.677
Really?

00:42:16.861 --> 00:42:18.192
What do you think?

00:42:18.229 --> 00:42:19.628
A boat.

00:42:19.663 --> 00:42:21.528
You said you wanted
to explore the river?

00:42:21.565 --> 00:42:22.964
I think I could build this.

00:42:23.000 --> 00:42:25.161
We could go on a camping trip.

00:42:25.202 --> 00:42:27.727
I'm not sure we could fit
the bathtub in the boat.

00:42:27.772 --> 00:42:29.296
Well, that's all right.
I'll have the river.

00:42:30.508 --> 00:42:31.907
Do you hear that?

00:42:31.942 --> 00:42:33.773
Yes.

00:42:37.248 --> 00:42:38.875
...to Captain Janeway.

00:42:38.916 --> 00:42:40.508
Do you read me?

00:42:40.551 --> 00:42:45.181
This is Tuvok calling Captain
Janeway and Commander Chakotay.

00:42:45.222 --> 00:42:47.588
Please respond.

00:42:47.625 --> 00:42:50.116
This is Janeway.

00:42:50.161 --> 00:42:52.721
Captain, it's good
to hear your voice.

00:42:52.763 --> 00:42:53.889
We have news.

00:42:53.931 --> 00:42:55.193
What is it?

00:42:55.232 --> 00:42:56.699
We have medicine
which we believe

00:42:56.734 --> 00:42:58.702
will effectively treat
your condition.

00:42:58.736 --> 00:43:02.001
We plan to be in orbit
within 30 hours.

00:43:16.887 --> 00:43:17.876
Ready?

00:43:27.031 --> 00:43:29.329
There you are.

00:43:31.001 --> 00:43:33.367
At least I get to say good-bye.

00:43:36.240 --> 00:43:39.334
Feel free to use the house.

00:43:52.857 --> 00:43:54.984
Janeway to Voyager.

00:43:55.025 --> 00:43:56.515
Two to beam up.

00:44:09.006 --> 00:44:10.439
Welcome back, Captain.

00:44:10.474 --> 00:44:11.907
Commander.

00:44:13.978 --> 00:44:15.240
The Doctor tells me

00:44:15.279 --> 00:44:17.747
you contacted the Vidiians
after all.

00:44:17.781 --> 00:44:19.772
I disobeyed your order, Captain.

00:44:19.817 --> 00:44:22.251
I am prepared to accept
the consequences.

00:44:22.286 --> 00:44:24.914
If I didn't know you better,

00:44:24.955 --> 00:44:28.482
I'd say your decision
was almost... emotional.

00:44:28.526 --> 00:44:30.391
Thank you all.

00:44:30.427 --> 00:44:31.621
Well, we've lost time
with all this.

00:44:31.662 --> 00:44:32.959
Let's see if we can make
some of it up.

00:44:32.997 --> 00:44:34.259
Mr. Paris, warp 8.

00:44:34.298 --> 00:44:35.094
Aye, Captain.

00:44:35.132 --> 00:44:36.121
Commander, we'll need

00:44:36.167 --> 00:44:37.429
to review
the ship's systems.

00:44:37.468 --> 00:44:39.732
I'll handle propulsion,
environmental and communication.

00:44:39.770 --> 00:44:40.862
You'll be responsible

00:44:40.905 --> 00:44:42.896
for sensors, weapons
and transporters.

00:44:42.940 --> 00:44:43.907
Aye, Captain.

00:44:43.941 --> 00:44:45.875
I'll have a report to you
by 1800 hours.

00:44:46.911 --> 00:44:48.139
Check with phaser maintenance.

00:44:48.179 --> 00:44:49.441
See if they solved that problem

00:44:49.480 --> 00:44:50.970
with the prefire
chamber temperature.

00:44:51.015 --> 00:44:52.073
Yes, ma'am.

00:44:52.116 --> 00:44:53.947
I'll see to it.
